{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Extend the dispatch cycle with lifecycle hooks — from invisible infrastructure to domain-specific features."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Swidux’s plugin system is a single protocol (","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxPlugin","type":"reference"},{"text":") with four lifecycle hooks and an ordered registry (","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost","type":"reference"},{"text":"). All store extensibility flows through this contract. The built-in ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","type":"reference"},{"text":" use it, and so do domain-specific features like killswitch enforcement and paywall management.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"The-Dispatch-Lifecycle","text":"The Dispatch Lifecycle"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Every call to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.send()"},{"text":" drives plugins through a four-phase lifecycle:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":null,"code":["plugins.willReduce(state:action:)      \/\/ 1. Pre-reduce (read-only state)","appReducer.reduce(state:action:...)    \/\/ 2. App reducer runs","pluginEffects = plugins.reduce(...)    \/\/ 3. Plugin reducers run","plugins.afterReduce(state:action:)     \/\/ 4. Post-reduce cleanup"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The generic ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store","type":"reference"},{"text":" implements this lifecycle internally. You don’t write ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"send()"},{"text":" by hand — ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store.send()"},{"text":" handles packing, reducing, plugin hooks, unpacking, and effect dispatch.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A fifth method, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flush()"},{"text":", runs once at shutdown to drain async buffers.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"All four hooks have default no-op implementations. Each plugin overrides only what it needs.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Core-Middleware-vs-Domain-Plugins","text":"Core Middleware vs Domain Plugins"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The plugin system serves two structurally different roles. Recognizing which one a plugin fills determines where it lives, which hooks it uses, and how it couples to the host app.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Core-Middleware","text":"Core Middleware"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","type":"reference"},{"text":" are ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"action-agnostic infrastructure"}]},{"text":". They never inspect the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Action"},{"text":" type, never dispatch actions, and never return effects. They couple only to the shape of state:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" needs keypaths to "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" properties."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" needs "},{"code":"State: Equatable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" so it can snapshot and compare."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Because they don’t touch actions, they work with any app that uses Swidux — no wiring required beyond construction.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Domain-Plugins","text":"Domain Plugins"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Killswitch, parental gate, and paywall plugins are ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"domain-specific modules"}]},{"text":" that ship as separate library targets (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxKillswitch"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxParentalGate"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPaywall"},{"text":"). They own their own state slices and action enums, dispatch effects, and must be explicitly wired into the host app’s root types.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each domain plugin stores three wiring pieces:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["private let stateKeyPath: WritableKeyPath<RootState, FeatureState>","private let toRootAction: @Sendable (FeatureAction) -> RootAction","private let extractAction: @Sendable (RootAction) -> FeatureAction?"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The host app provides these at init — the plugin never assumes a specific root type.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Comparison","text":"Comparison"},{"type":"table","header":"row","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Core Middleware"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Domain Plugins"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Action knowledge"}]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"None"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Full — extracts and lifts actions"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Lifecycle hooks"}]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willReduce"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce"},{"type":"text","text":" only"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Returns effects"}]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"State coupling"}]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keypath to "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"type":"text","text":" constraint"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keypath to plugin’s own state slice"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Wiring"}]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Construction only"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keypath + action lifter + action extractor"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Target"}],"type":"strong"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Core "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Swidux"},{"type":"text","text":" library"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Separate library target"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Opt-in"}]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Instantiate and register"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add state, action case, and register"}]}]]]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"The-Decision-Rule","text":"The Decision Rule"},{"type":"aside","style":"important","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Does the middleware need to know your action type? If "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"no","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":", it’s core middleware — put it in "},{"code":"Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and use ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willReduce"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"},{"text":". If ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"yes","type":"text"}]},{"text":", it’s a domain plugin — give it its own target and use ","type":"text"},{"code":"reduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}],"name":"Important"},{"anchor":"Hook-Selection-Guide","level":2,"text":"Hook Selection Guide","type":"heading"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willReduce(state:action:)"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" — Capture state "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"before"}]},{"type":"text","text":" the reducer mutates it. State is read-only. Use for snapshots (undo) or pre-mutation analytics."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce(state:action:) -> Effect?"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — Handle domain-specific actions ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"after"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" the app reducer. Mutate the plugin’s state slice and return effects. This is the only hook that can dispatch actions or do async work.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce(state:action:)"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — Observe state ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"after","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" all reducing is done. Use for persistence draining, logging, or metrics. Cannot return effects.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flush() async"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — Shutdown hook. Flush pending async buffers (persistence writes, analytics batches). Called once when the app exits.","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"anchor":"Registration-Order","level":2,"text":"Registration Order","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" executes plugins in registration order. Recommended ordering:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let plugins = PluginHost<AppState, AppAction>()","plugins.register(undoPlugin)         \/\/ 1. Must snapshot before any mutation","plugins.register(persistencePlugin)  \/\/ 2. Drains changelogs after reducer","plugins.register(killswitchPlugin)   \/\/ 3. Domain plugins in any order","plugins.register(paywallPlugin)"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Undo must come first — it snapshots state in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willReduce"},{"type":"text","text":", before the app reducer or any plugin modifies it. Persistence typically comes next so its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"},{"type":"text","text":" drain sees the final state. Domain plugins use only "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce"},{"type":"text","text":", so their relative order rarely matters."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Service-Result-Actions-and-Transition-Observation","level":2,"text":"Service-Result Actions and Transition Observation","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"service-result action"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":"’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"customerInfoUpdated"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"KillswitchPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":"’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"verdictReceived"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FeatureFlagsPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":"’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refreshSucceeded"},{"type":"text","text":" — fires on "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"every"}]},{"type":"text","text":" fetch, refresh, or stream tick, not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"only when the value changed, and unconditionally writes its payload to the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"state slice. The payload is frequently identical to what is already there","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(a re-delivered entitlement, an unchanged remote config).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Do "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"not"}]},{"text":" map analytics or side effects to the raw service-result action:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it fires duplicates by design. Observe the ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"state slice"}]},{"text":" — or a value","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"derived from it — instead.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"State observation is already deduplicated by the framework. ","type":"text"},{"code":"Store.send","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"packs the observer into a value-type snapshot, lets reducers mutate the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"snapshot, then writes back via ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"State.apply"},{"text":". For a leaf slice that write","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"is a plain assignment whose "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"text":" setter equality-gates ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"values, so a slice whose value did not change emits no notification — and a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"value-diffing consumer such as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsIdentity.userProperties"},{"type":"text","text":" (which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsPlugin"},{"text":" re-evaluates and diffs every non-analytics dispatch) sees exactly the","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"real transitions. This dedup is a property of the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store"},{"type":"text","text":", not of any"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"per-plugin guard, so a no-op service-result cycle is silent to state"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"observers without any extra reducer logic."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Next-Steps","level":2,"text":"Next Steps"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" — Step-by-step guide to creating a domain plugin","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" — Configure the built-in persistence middleware"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" — Add undo\/redo with the built-in undo middleware"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginarchitecture"]}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","title":"Plugin Architecture"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Explanation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/DesignPrinciples"],"title":"Explanation"}],"kind":"article","sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoPlugin":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoplugin","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"UndoPlugin"}],"title":"UndoPlugin","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"UndoPlugin"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Snapshot-based undo\/redo plugin."}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistencemiddlewareguide","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","role":"article","title":"Persistence Middleware","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Configure automatic persistence that drains entity changes and batches database writes."}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/BuildingADomainPlugin":{"abstract":[{"text":"Create a self-contained feature plugin with its own state, actions, and effects.","type":"text"}],"role":"article","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/buildingadomainplugin","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin","kind":"article","title":"Building a Domain Plugin"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/SwiduxPlugin":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A plugin that participates in the Swidux dispatch cycle."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SwiduxPlugin"}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SwiduxPlugin"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/swiduxplugin","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxPlugin","kind":"symbol","title":"SwiduxPlugin"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/EntityStore":{"abstract":[{"text":"An ordered, keyed collection of identifiable entities that silently records","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"every mutation for downstream persistence.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityStore"}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityStore"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystore","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","kind":"symbol","title":"EntityStore"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistencePlugin":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistenceplugin","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"PersistencePlugin"}],"title":"PersistencePlugin","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"PersistencePlugin"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Coalescing persistence plugin."}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/DesignPrinciples":{"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/DesignPrinciples","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/designprinciples","title":"Design Principles","type":"topic","kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"The 10 rules that shape every Swidux app, and the reasoning behind them.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginHost":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginhost","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"PluginHost","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"PluginHost","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"PluginHost"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Ordered registry of plugins that drives the dispatch lifecycle."}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoRedo":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Add stack-based undo\/redo to your app with "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"role":"article","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoredo","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","kind":"article","title":"Undo \/ Redo"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"abstract":[{"text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates.","type":"text"}],"role":"collection","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","kind":"symbol","title":"Swidux"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Store":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/store","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Store"}],"title":"Store","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Store"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Generic store that owns the dispatch cycle, plugin lifecycle, and"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"observation layer.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/ArchitectureGuide":{"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/architectureguide","title":"Architecture & Performance","type":"topic","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Understand the architectural patterns that make Swidux work correctly with SwiftUI’s observation system."}]}}}